2081A - Math Division Idea: Ecrade_ Hint 1 Consider $x$ in binary form. Hint 2 What are all possible numbers of operations to make $x$ equal to $1$? Hint 3 Consider using dynamic programming to calculate the answer. Solution Similar to the previous problem, the possible number of operations can only be $n-1$ or $n$, depending on whether a carry-over occurs in $x$ during the $(n-1)$ -th operation. We can use dynamic programming to compute the probability of a carry-over occurring during the $(n-1)$ -th operation. Let $f_i$ denote the probability of a carry-over occurring at the $i$ -th least significant bit. The recurrence relation is: $ f_i = \begin{cases} \dfrac{1}{2} \times f_{i-1} & x_i = 0 \\ \dfrac{1}{2} \times (1 - f_{i-1}) + f_{i-1} & x_i = 1 \end{cases} $ The final answer is given by $n-1+f_{n-1}$. The time complexity is $O(\sum n)$. Code

