2085B - Serval and Final MEX Hint 1 Before the last operation, what should the array be to obtain $0$? Hint 2 How to make all the elements in the array non-zero? Solution Note that before the last operation, all the integers in the array should be positive. Thus, we aim to turn the zeroes in $a$ into non-zeroes. To achieve this, we split the given array $a$ into two halves and perform the operations on the halves that contain zeroes. After that, there will be no zeroes in either of the two halves. The final $0$ can be obtained by performing the last operation on the entire array. $ [{\color{red}{\underline{1, 0, 1, 1}}}, {\color{blue}{2, 0, 8, 5}}] \to [{\color{red}{2}}, {\color{blue}{\underline{2, 0, 8, 5}}}] \to [\underline{{\color{red}{2}}, {\color{blue}{1}}}] \to [0] $ Another Hint In fact, the final element can be $0$ after the operations for any array of length $4$. Can you solve the problem under the constraint of $n=4$? Another Solution When $n \gt 4$, you can perform the operation on any subarray of length $(n-3)$. After the operation, the array $a$ will contain only $4$ integers, which can be solved by brute force. Code (Python)

