The first line contains an integer $t$ ($1 \le t \le 10^4$) — the number of testcases. The first line of each testcase contains an integer $n$ ($1 \le n \le 2 \cdot 10^5$) — the length of $a$. The second line of each testcase contains $n$ integers $a_1,a_2,\ldots,a_n$ ($-10^9 \le a_i \le 10^9$, $a_i \ne 0$). The sum of $n$ across all testcases does not exceed $2 \cdot 10^5$.

[Output]
